.TH APPATTIC\-QT 1 "2026-09-27" "appattic-qt 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
appattic\-qt \- Qt 6 window for leftover, stale app, package and disk scans
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B appattic-qt
.RB [ --version ]
.RB [ --help ]
.RB [ --smoke ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B appattic\-qt
is the Linux window of AppAttic. It shows leftovers from uninstalled apps,
stale installed apps, outdated versions, unused distro and language packages,
and disk usage. Nothing is deleted until a script is reviewed in the window
or the move is confirmed.
.PP
Package-manager queries run on the host. As a Flatpak they are spawned with
.B flatpak-spawn --host
and plugin tags are read from
.IR /run/host ;
installed as a plain CMake or AppImage package they run directly. Scan plugins
cannot delete files or run a distro upgrade.
.PP
The WASM modules are read from
.IR $APPATTIC_CORE_OUT ,
or from
.I ../share/appattic
next to the binary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR --help ", " \-h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B --smoke
Run the headless smoke test and exit. Prints
.B SMOKE=ok
on success. Useful with
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen
on a host with no display server.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B APPATTIC_CORE_OUT
Directory holding the compiled WASM modules.
.TP
.B WASMTIME_DIR
Wasmtime C API prefix used at build time, not at run time.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The window closed normally, or the requested option completed.
.TP
.B 1
The scan failed, or the smoke test failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/appattic/settings.json
Confirm-before-running and ignored leftover paths. Include-system-apps is a macOS-only setting; the Linux window does not scan installed system apps.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and
.I https://github.com/maci0/appattic
for the full scan description.
